{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>תרתי.</b> When I saw that wisdom alone begets pain, and laughter alone is of no benefit, I sought a way to combine the two, and I drew my flesh with wine, so that I might rejoice. And the meaning of 'my flesh' is my body." "<b>And my heart guides in wisdom.</b> My heart in place of my intellect and my soul. And 'guides' is a transitive verb [פועל יוצא], and the object [הפעול] is missing [חסר], its meaning being: my heart guides its affairs in wisdom, and takes hold of a little of folly, which is the desire of this world. And all this, until it might show which is the good way."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:01.827659372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}